      "id": "9-genuine-conflicting-authority",
      "description": "CORRECTED by PHASE-10A1-R1: a raw conflict.hasConflict:true boolean alone is incomplete evidence under the renderer/compliance conflictMetadataIsComplete() standard (no conflictType/exactIssue/oppositeHoldingGate/resolutionBasis), so it must NOT be exposed as a verified, user-displayable conflict. It maps to conflictState POTENTIAL_CONFLICT, hasConflict:false, and authoritySupport falls through to the normal AUTHORITY_FOUND+displayed-cards evaluation (VERIFIED_CONTROLLING). The evidence is not discarded -- it is surfaced via limitations:[\"POTENTIAL_CONFLICT\"].",
      "input": {
        "responseType": "rag_answer",
        "sourceStatus": "AUTHORITY_FOUND",
        "displayedSourceCount": 2,
        "conflict": {
          "hasConflict": true
        },
        "answerSupport": {
